Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:42:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Video] Fix missing movie information within sets (#29736)

Movies with versions or extras are represented as folders. When accessed
within a movie set, the information handler incorrectly identifies these
folders as sets based on their path.

This bypasses full movie-detail loading, leaving the cast list empty and
the Refresh button unavailable.

Check the item's video content type instead of its path to distinguish
movie sets from movie folders.

Tested with Alien in a Windows Debug build: cast and Refresh display
correctly with movie-set grouping both enabled and disabled.

(cherry picked from commit 1a7630c092c1c786789e47ef5731d09b4de78b81)
---
 xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp b/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
index 2584ba7..1f18158 100644
--- a/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
@@ -243,8 +243,7 @@ bool CGUIWindowVideoBase::OnItemInfo(const CFileItem& fileItem)
 
   // Movie set
   if (fileItem.IsFolder() && VIDEO::IsVideoDb(fileItem) &&
-      fileItem.GetPath() != "videodb://movies/sets/" &&
-      StringUtils::StartsWith(fileItem.GetPath(), "videodb://movies/sets/"))
+      fileItem.GetVideoContentType() == VideoDbContentType::MOVIE_SETS)
     return ShowInfoAndRefresh(std::make_shared<CFileItem>(fileItem), nullptr);
 
   // Music video. Match visibility test of CMusicInfo::IsVisible
